<!-- Exercise 007 - LayoutWrapPanel (beginner).
     Goal:   Let four fixed-width tiles wrap onto two rows.
     Drills: WrapPanel wrapping at a constrained width.
     Passes: dotnet test, filtered to Ex007_ (see the exact command in
     Ex007_LayoutWrapPanel.axaml.cs - an XML comment may not hold two hyphens
     in a row, so it cannot appear here). -->
<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="FeWoLearning.Avalonia.Exercises.Beginner.Ex007_LayoutWrapPanel">
  <!-- TODO: replace this placeholder with a horizontal WrapPanel named "ItemsPanel":
         Width 200, pinned to the top-left,
         holding four Borders named "Item1".."Item4", each 80 wide and 20 tall.
       Two tiles fit per row at 200 wide (160 fits, 240 does not), so Item3 and
       Item4 must wrap onto a second row.
       The test looks up the panel by that name and checks it really is a
       WrapPanel constrained to 200 wide - a Grid or Canvas with hand-picked
       positions could otherwise reproduce the same four rectangles without
       ever using wrapping, the mechanism this exercise drills. -->
  <TextBlock Text="TODO" />
</UserControl>
